<title>JAPAN: Japan Oct domestic vehicle output up 12.3% yr/yr. [CORRECTED 06:17 GMT]</title>
<headline>Japan Oct domestic vehicle output up 12.3% yr/yr. [CORRECTED 06:17 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's vehicle production in October rose 12.3 percent from a year earlier to 941,461 vehicles, the Japan Automobile Manufacturers' Association (JAMA) said on Monday.</p>
<p>It was the second successive month of year-on-year gains.  </p>
<p>A breakdown of the figures with percentage changes follows:</p>
<p>					 OCT	     YR/YR PCT</p>
<p> Cars				734,642	    +17.2</p>
<p> Trucks			    202,801	     -2.2</p>
<p> Buses				 4,018	     -3.7</p>
<p> Total			     941,461	    +12.3</p>
<p>October production by major manufacturers:</p>
<p>					 OCT	    YR/YR PCT</p>
<p> Toyota Motor Corp	     337,181	     +20.2</p>
<p> Nissan Motor Co Ltd	   132,698	     -5.6</p>
<p> Mitsubishi Motors Corp	102,073	     +6.2</p>
<p> Honda Motor Co Ltd	    108,691	    +40.3</p>
<p> Mazda Motor Corp		 67,272	    +21.6</p>
<p>(Corrects the year-on-year percentage change figures in the table for the five major manufacturers.)</p>
